  "id": "carbohydrate-metabolism",
  "term": "carbohydrate metabolism",
  "definition": "Carbohydrate metabolism is the set of body processes that produce and use glucose, involving organs such as the stomach, intestine, liver, kidney, muscles, adipose tissue, brain, and heart. It includes pathways like glucose oxidation, glycolysis, and gluconeogenesis, and is influenced by insulin and insulin resistance.",
